# Generated Code Rules

Generated code is not automatically correct code.

- Keep generated artefacts clearly separated from handwritten hooks/behaviour.
- Never hand-edit generated files unless the generator explicitly requires it.
- Generator inputs and overrides must be reviewable.
- Encode domain-specific operational knowledge via explicit hooks/policies rather than opaque post-generation patches.
- Generated resources must still satisfy reconciliation, security, adoption, deletion, and status conventions.
- For k8sbricks, evaluate reuse/adaptation of an existing controller generator before inventing a generator from scratch.
- A generator spike must prove one representative resource family end-to-end before committing to the architecture.
